WEBVTT

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:09.360
London, 1939

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:08.510
I spy you.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.390
You're under arrest for espionage.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.140
<i>As the embers of world war 
smoldered in autumn of 1937,</i>

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.500
<i>the Imperial Army established</i>

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:27.190
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.660
<i>a clandestine spy training agency.</i>

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:30.480
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:33.460
<i>The histories, names, and even ages</i>

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:37.280
<i>of the elite men who pass its 
rigorous application process</i>

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.930
<i>are all treated as top-secret information.</i>

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.500
<i>They easily complete training 
exercises that push them</i>

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.500
<i>to their physical and mental limits.</i>

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.710
<i>Under the command of founder 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki,</i>

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.000
<i>they operate worldwide, within the shadows.</i>

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:56.710
<i>And so a brand-new intelligence 
agency was created.</i>

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.720
<i>Its name is "D-Agency."</i>

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:41.240
Episode 5 - Robinson

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.540
<i>Robinson Crusoe, born in York, England,</i>

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:45.210
<i>set sail for adventure, 
despite his father's warnings.</i>

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:52.620
This program is a work of fiction. 
The characters, organizations, locations, laws, names, 
etc. being portrayed are unrelated to actual events.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.140
<i>He was shipwrecked in a storm, 
but was fortunate enough to survive,</i>

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:55.030
<i>and washed ashore on an uninhabited island.</i>

00:03:55.670 --> 00:04:00.560
<i>Using the few tools left in his possession,
he built himself a house,</i>

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:03.940
<i>grew grains, and hardily carried on.</i>

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:08.100
<i>Twenty-five years after 
washing ashore on the island,</i>

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:13.950
<i>Robinson saved a young savage on the 
verge of being killed by cannibals.</i>

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.780
<i>Robinson named the young man "Friday,"</i>

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:20.230
<i>because that was the day on which he saved him.</i>

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:27.930
A parting gift. Take it.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:38.000
<i>Though saved from solitude by Friday,</i>

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.080
<i>Robinson was forced to spend 28 years</i>

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.880
<i>on the uninhabited island.</i>

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.300
<i>Is he telling me to be prepared</i>

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:49.160
<i>for this mission to last that long?</i>

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.230
What do you want?

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:31.250
This is a mistake! You've got the wrong man!

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.540
Sorry for the rough treatment.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.590
Let's see, you are...

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:39.070
Izawa Kazuo.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:41.050
I'm a photographer.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:44.740
Maeda London Photo Studio?

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.200
Yes, on Oxford Street.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:50.090
Ah, that's the studio

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:52.160
near the tube station.

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:53.930
Yes...

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:56.680
I visit the pub near there quite often

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.170
to drink a stout.

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:02.080
R-Right, I frequent that pub, too...

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:06.220
Do you have any idea why 
you were brought here?

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:10.300
No, I haven't the faintest.

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:15.390
You're suspected of being a Japanese spy.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.470
A spy? Me?

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.150
That's ridiculous.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:25.190
I'm just a photographer.

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:27.830
If you don't believe me, ask my uncle—

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:34.140
We've had you under surveillance 
for over two weeks.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:38.150
German spies, members of 
the British Union of Fascists...

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:44.250
That's rather odd company for a simple 
photographer to keep, don't you think?

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.470
What are you talking about?

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:57.890
I don't understand at all.

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:02.460
I haven't even been in London for a month...

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:04.830
Yes, we've heard.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:09.320
We're interested in the real 
reason you came to London.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:13.280
I'm telling you, I'm taking 
over for my sick uncle—

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.580
We've heard that, too.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:18.640
I swear to God, I don't know 
what you're talking about.

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:21.670
Very well.

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:24.220
Let's take a break.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:26.390
Clearly, this will be a long day.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:29.190
Go and visit the restroom.

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:41.960
Can we get more men sent to the north side?

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.230
Roger that.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:46.330
The retrieval is going to 
take another three weeks.

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:47.240
Got it.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:48.700
Also...

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.480
What...

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:02.250
Now, let's continue.

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.020
Do you know what this is?

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:58.890
<b>Army Intelligence 
Codebook Volume 3</b>

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:04.990
I envy Yuuki for having an 
exemplary subordinate like you.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:08.710
<i>Lieutenant Colonel Howard Marks...</i>

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:12.040
<i>The British Secret Intelligence 
Service's spymaster.</i>

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:14.210
I'm afraid time is up.

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:17.250
We can't take things slowly any longer.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:25.460
This is the latest truth serum we've developed.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:28.350
It will tell us much more about

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:31.230
your real self than any amount of torture.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:42.290
Oh, don't worry.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:46.860
We know how capable you are, 
and how loyal you are to your country.

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:03.370
Well, in that case, I can say this...

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:09.060
This is a secret. Keep this to yourself, okay?

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:15.850
You know the Maeda London 
Photo studio, on Oxford Street?

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:20.550
Do you know who that voice belongs to?

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:22.630
Sotomura Hitoshi.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:25.890
A diplomat who just arrived in London.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:31.810
The old man, Maeda, who ran 
the place, returned to Japan.

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:35.560
And his young nephew who 
came here to take over...

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:39.500
Listen, you seriously can't 
tell anyone about this.

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:44.280
Look, if you don't trust me, fine.

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:45.860
Don't be like that.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:49.450
Anyway, this guy from Japan, Izawa Kazuo,

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.100
<i>Stop.</i>

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:52.440
is actually a Japanese spy.

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:51.640
<i>Shut up.</i>

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:55.330
Are you serious?

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:56.630
Listen.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:59.330
There's this top-secret organization in

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:01.930
the Japanese Imperial Army called "D-Agency."

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:01.930
<i>Stop it...</i>

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:05.910
Only a select few in the Ministry of 
Foreign Affairs even know it exists.

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.810
He was deployed here to...

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:15.310
Do you understand the situation 
you're in right now?

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:19.780
I've been... sold out.

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:25.750
Any idea who blew your cover?

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:28.410
Yuuki...

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.100
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:31.830
Okay.

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:37.500
Now we're getting somewhere.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.210
How're you feeling?

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:48.190
Use me.

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:49.540
Hm?

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:52.900
Use me.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:55.470
Finally changed your mind, have you?

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:59.830
I've got nowhere to go back to.

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:02.650
You make a most pleasing offer.

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:05.610
You're a man sold out by Yuuki.

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:08.230
There's no better letter of credit

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:11.470
to earn our trust than this.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:13.620
As I asked you earlier,

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:16.590
<b>Army Intelligence 
Codebook Volume 3</b>

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:16.310
do you know what this is?

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:20.060
A codebook.

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:24.170
A Japanese Imperial Army codebook.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:25.820
Indeed.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:27.860
And going with that...

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:39.870
We've already got a task 
we want you to perform.

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:49.750
Your first job is

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:53.750
to use this to send a coded telegram to Japan.

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:57.300
We've already prepared 
the telegram's contents.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:01.990
We've also already encoded the message

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:03.740
and converted it to Morse code.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:07.650
You simply need to send the message using

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:10.040
the unique keying style assigned to you.

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:11.060
Sir.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:19.200
What's wrong?

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:21.800
You said it yourself a minute ago.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:24.670
Yuuki sold you out.

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:28.200
You have no other options left.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:56.810
Now you are openly

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:58.770
one of our allies.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:02.230
Take him to get some food.

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:03.040
Sir.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:07.020
Don't forget the handcuffs.

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:07.990
Handcuffs?

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:11.930
Until we can confirm that our fake intel

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:14.060
has done actual damage to Japan,

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:17.460
we can't allow him to leave here.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.920
Don't let him out of your sight.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.670
Yes, sir. My apologies.

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:40.360
Hey.

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:42.730
I need to use the restroom.

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:44.360
To your right.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:52.420
Isn't the one around that corner closer?

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:56.090
How did you know that?

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:18.020
What's wrong? What happened?

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:21.130
What?

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:24.440
What's in the mirror?

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:43.030
<i>I confirmed the restroom 
locations just in case,</i>

00:15:43.030 --> 00:15:44.400
<i>and it seems I was correct.</i>

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:58.710
<i>There's an emergency staircase 
at the end of the third floor.</i>

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:00.440
<i>If I can get out through there...</i>

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:05.530
<i>I should come out on the storeroom 
rooftop to escape on the main road.</i>

00:16:16.570 --> 00:16:19.780
<i>Right around that corner is the 
door to the emergency stairway!</i>

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:32.300
<i>No... Why?</i>

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:37.550
<i>That was a trap?!</i>

00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:41.760
<i>I'm working against a British SIS spymaster.</i>

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:45.350
<i>A trap of that level should've 
been well within my expectations.</i>

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.640
<i>Is this the end?</i>

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.250
The prisoner's escaped!

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:52.870
Upstairs! He's up there!

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:53.970
Third floor!

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:05.060
Okay, he's on this floor.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:08.690
He's trapped. I'll come in from behind.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:11.630
Show yourself! You've got nowhere to run!

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.390
Don't waste time hiding! Come out!

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:34.620
Well? Did you find him?

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:40.280
No, he's not in here!

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:45.040
What the hell? There's 
no sign of him anywhere!

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:46.700
Where'd he disappear to?

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.430
What's going on?

00:17:48.430 --> 00:17:52.080
Sir, we trapped him on this 
floor, but he's vanished.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:55.110
The floors below are completely secured.

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:57.590
We'll just secure each floor 
until we corner him above.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:17:59.830
But above here is...

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.500
We know he's inside somewhere.

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:04.150
He's not on this floor, correct?

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:06.910
No, sir. We checked every room.

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:10.090
<i>Though Robinson Crusoe</i>

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:13.130
<i>lived alone on the uninhabited island,</i>

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:16.000
<i>he continued to act the 
part of an Englishman.</i>

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:17.530
<i>The perfect allegory</i>

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:20.020
<i>of a spy who's infiltrated an enemy country,</i>

00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:22.000
<i>who never reveals the slightest truth</i>

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:25.360
<i>even to the friends and family 
he gains while living there,</i>

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:29.100
<i>but remains nonchalant the whole time.</i>

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:32.790
<i>Twenty-five years after 
washing ashore on the island,</i>

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:36.520
<i>Robinson saved a young man on the verge</i>

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:38.030
<i>of being killed by cannibals.</i>

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:40.660
<i>Robinson named the young man "Friday,"</i>

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:43.940
<i>because that was the day on which he saved him.</i>

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:49.010
<i>Normally, he probably works as</i>

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:51.250
<i>a loyal soldier to His Majesty the King,</i>

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:56.100
<i>and only activates when the SIS 
captures a Japanese spy.</i>

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:59.210
<i>A sleeping spy, a sleeper.</i>

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:01.780
<i>And "Friday," the code for him,</i>

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:05.310
<i>is represented by the 
astronomical sign for Venus.</i>

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:07.390
<i>That planetary symbol...</i>

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:14.830
<i>Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki didn't 
inform me of Friday's existence.</i>

00:19:14.830 --> 00:19:17.700
<i>You can't confess what you don't know.</i>

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:20.780
What I'm asking of you men is simply

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:23.300
to split your consciousness 
into multiple levels.

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:26.040
Information the enemy can have 
stays on the top level.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:29.140
Information they can't is 
put in the lower levels.

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:31.150
It's child's play.

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:35.920
<i>When Lieutenant Colonel Marks ordered 
me to send that false information,</i>

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:40.230
<i>I relayed his message verbatim, with no errors.</i>

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:44.730
<i>A perfectly keyed coded message...</i>

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:48.430
<i>To D-Agency, that signals trouble 
encountered behind enemy lines.</i>

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:51.710
<i>It means, "I'm captured. Send help."</i>

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:56.710
<i>Obviously, this info is stored in
the deepest level of my mind,</i>

00:19:57.080 --> 00:20:01.270
<i>so deep that I'd have to be killed 
before anyone could extract it.</i>

00:20:12.240 --> 00:20:14.140
Can you give me a light?

00:20:14.670 --> 00:20:16.430
My shoes are black.

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:28.600
When the enemy captures an enemy spy

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:31.850
or deciphers the enemy's codes,

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:35.460
they'll immediately be possessed by an urge

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:39.670
to use the captured spy to send 
false intel back to the enemy.

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:42.610
And that very moment

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:45.370
will be your chance to escape.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:48.080
<i>Three months ago,</i>

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:52.390
<i>we learned that confidential Imperial Army 
intel was being leaked to the British.</i>

00:20:52.670 --> 00:20:54.710
<i>A diplomat in London</i>

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:57.400
<i>hadn't been encoding his communications.</i>

00:20:58.140 --> 00:21:00.860
<i>The army immediately 
protested, demanding that</i>

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:03.140
<i>all communications on 
military matters be encoded.</i>

00:21:03.140 --> 00:21:04.590
<i>But due to the incidents,</i>

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:07.320
<i>they were unable to connect 
the leak to the diplomat,</i>

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:10.750
<i>so the Ministry of Foreign Affairs 
repeatedly ignored the army's requests.</i>

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:16.300
<i>However, if I were captured in Britain 
because a diplomat leaked my identity,</i>

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:18.930
<i>that would clearly put Foreign Affairs at fault.</i>

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:21.160
<i>Faced with such irrefutable evidence,</i>

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:24.010
<i>the Ministry would have to listen to the army.</i>

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:28.770
<i>That was the scenario Lieutenant 
Colonel Yuuki wrote.</i>

00:21:30.900 --> 00:21:33.820
<i>I wonder where I'll end up next.</i>

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:23.840
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:24.110 --> 00:23:26.710
You always handle the cards very deftly.

00:23:27.580 --> 00:23:30.230
It's not the cards I'm manipulating.

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:34.880
Episode 6 - Asia Express

00:23:32.920 --> 00:23:34.510
It's your heart.
